{
  "timestamp": "2026-08-27T14:54:01Z",
  "title": "Rebuild nadiaeldeib.com",
  "type": "feature",
  "userRequest": "sounds good, soften the language as you proposed. write out the build plan.",
  "description": "Built the approved Night Field design as a working Next.js site: one route composed of six numbered sections (Work, About, Writing, Adventures, Elsewhere, Contact), 17 photographs cross-fading on a shared eight-second slot so every rotation lands on one beat, and a contact form that writes its row before attempting delivery, so a note survives a mail outage with emailedAt left null rather than being lost. There is deliberately no email address anywhere on the site; the form is the way in. Extraction pulled the decision logic out of the components into tested units (validateMessage, splitOnBrand, submitMessage, pickActive) and split every section into sub-components, covered by 55 component scenarios and 1 application scenario. 36 tests pass and the audit is clean.\n\nTwo real defects surfaced and were fixed. The contact form's own default chip was rejected: the validator restated the topic allow-list by hand as 'working-together' while the form submits 'consulting', so anyone who never touched the chips got a 422. The list now derives from content/site.json, with a regression test that submits every chip the form actually offers. Separately, all six PhotoRotator scenarios were capturing blank frames, because the isolation-route wrapper used width:100% inside a centered flex container and collapsed to zero width; text components survived on their intrinsic width, but the rotator's absolutely-positioned images had none. Fixed to explicit widths and recaptured, and the rotator scenario set was then differentiated by frame count (1, 2, 3, 4, 6, and empty) so each selects a distinct keyframe set and opens on a distinct photograph, since a capture freezes the first frame.\n\nSCOPE VERDICT. Delivered: (1) rebuild nadiaeldeib.com as a fresh site carrying over the existing content, (2) redesign the aesthetic with new typography, color, layout and motion rather than a reskin, (3) explore multiple design directions across rounds and lock one in, which produced six mockups with 03 selected and 01 parked in history/01-clean-direction/. Deferred: (4) publish live at nadiaeldeib.com and (5) point nseldeib.com at the same site. Both deferrals are user-planned, not agent-decided: both rows are marked assist-track non-build, and the user's own build plan sequences deploy after commit, since it still needs Resend wiring, a SQLite to Postgres swap for Vercel, and adopting the nadia-website remote. Nothing was deferred without the user's decision.\n\nOne environmental limitation to record: preview-verify could not run for this entire session. The editor process advertises 127.0.0.1:14350, pinned by open-codeyam.sh, but is bound to 54407, and that value lives in the running process, so no config file reaches it and restart-server does not clear it. A structural exception was recorded at the Demo step. Every other path, including component capture, scenario registration, and the full-page screenshot, resolves the correct port and works.",
